  "question": {
    "text": "The density of ' \\(x\\) ' \\(\\mathrm{M}\\) solution (' \\(X\\) ' molar) of \\(\\mathrm{NaOH}\\) is \\(1.12 \\mathrm{~g} \\mathrm{~mL}^{-1}\\), while in molality, the concentration of the solution is \\(3 \\mathrm{~m}(3 \\mathrm{molal})\\). Then \\(x\\) is (Given : Molar mass of \\(\\mathrm{NaOH}\\) is \\(40 \\mathrm{~g} / \\mathrm{mol}\\) )",
    "image": null
  },
